1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
IronVision AI: human-approved AI for the NIST Risk Management Framework.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:13,000
This is a shared demonstration workspace with synthetic data only, one click from sign-in.

3
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:20,000
Personas let one presenter act as ISSO, assessor or AO; the active role is always shown.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:31,000
The RMF overview is the command center: all seven NIST 800-37 steps, computed from live records.

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Navigation follows the RMF steps, with the Import Center and Policies one click away.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Every screen works on the selected system, shown at the top.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:56,000
The Import Center takes eMASS workbooks, test results, inventories, scans and policies, and detects each file's type.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Here a synthetic eMASS Control Information export is imported into the current system.

9
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Review shows every change before it lands: current value, imported value, and anything that needs a decision.

10
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Conflict-free changes are accepted in one step and applied through the normal save paths, with full audit.

11
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Manage imported data shows everything one import populated, grouped by section, with the value before and after.

12
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Restore, clear or delete per field, per section, or everything the import created. The system itself is kept.

13
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Every operation can be undone for thirty days, and approved decisions are never removed, only flagged for re-review.

14
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Destination screens mark imported rows with their source file, with multi-select delete and undo.

15
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:32,000
The Policy Auditor checks each policy against every control requirement, reading the whole document.

16
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:44,000
No silent misses: a requirement is only reported missing after a second look finds nothing.

17
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Otherwise it says needs manual review, with confidence and the closest candidate passages.

18
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:05,000
If the reviewer finds the language, Found it here records the passage for a human mapping decision.

19
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Scan findings arrive hashed, deduplicated and mapped through CCIs to NIST 800-53 controls.

20
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:30,000
The authorization package brings the SSP, assessment results, POA&Ms and OSCAL exports together.

21
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:45,000
The decision is AO-only: the ISSO submits, the ISSM endorses, and separation of duties is enforced.

22
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Continuous monitoring watches evidence freshness, CAT I findings, CISA KEV and overdue POA&Ms.

23
00:03:55,500 --> 00:04:10,000
The Evidence Ledger keeps every artifact with its SHA-256 hash, provenance and versions.

24
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:25,000
Traceability links each control to evidence, findings, POA&Ms and assessments.

25
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:38,000
From preparation to continuous monitoring, the whole lifecycle stays in one place.

26
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:50,000
IronVision AI: AI does the heavy lifting; people keep the authority.

27
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:59,500
